		"nodes": {
			"18": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EDGE DETECTION\n\nThe Edge Detection node tries to see what the outlines of your texture is and produces lines where it detects them. \nThere are a few different ways to calculate this, for this we have the algorithm inlet. \nYour best bet is to just try them all and see what looks best.\n\nColor select determines what values of the texture are targeted by the algorithms. S\ntrength sets how strong the effect is.\n\nSample offset will determine in which direction the lines are sampled.\nThe first value is for the X axis and the second value is for the Y axis. \n\nThe High Quality mode can be enabled either in the node panel or on the node. \nThis enables the Edge Detection node to sample in both directions. \nSo an X of 1 will be a 1 pixel line on both the left and the right side of the line. \nAlthough this is cool, it is more taxing on your GPU and is therfore disabled by default."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 346.4189453125,
					"width": 817.92864990234375,
					"x": 177.2471466064453125,
					"y": -84.8714141845703125
				},
				"class": {
